    <statement><p>(a) Set up a double integral for calculating
the flux of the vector field
<m>\vec{F}(x,y,z) = z^2 \vec{k}</m> 
through the upper hemisphere of the sphere  
<m>x^2+y^2+z^2 = 9</m>, oriented away from the 
origin.  If necessary, enter 
<m>\rho</m> as <em>rho,</em>
<m>\theta</m> as <em>theta,</em> and
<m>\phi</m> as <em>phi.</em></p>
<p>Flux = <m>\displaystyle \int_{A}^{B} \!\! \int_{C}^{D}</m>
<fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/>
<m>d\phi \, d\theta</m></p>
<p>A = <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>B = <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p>C = <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
<p>D = <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
<p>(b) Evaluate the integral.</p>
<p>Flux = 
<m>\displaystyle \iint\limits_S \vec{F} \cdot d\vec{A}</m> =
<fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0006"/></p>
</statement>
    <hint><m>z = \rho \cos(\phi)</m>.


</hint>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3^{4}\cos^{3}\mathopen{}\left(phi\right)\sin\mathopen{}\left(phi\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2\pi </m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{\pi }{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{\pi \cdot 3^{4}}{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
